# TeckFirm WiFi

Work phase by phase. Do not implement Paystack charges until that phase.

- TypeScript strict mode. Avoid `any`.
- Business logic belongs in `src/services`. External APIs belong in `src/lib/paystack` and `src/lib/omada`.
- Never trust payment amounts from the frontend. Never assume a Paystack callback means success.
- One verified payment must never create multiple vouchers. Use unique constraints and fulfillment locks.
- Omada uses Cloud Access only (`euw1-api-omada-controller-connector.tplinkcloud.com` for the OC200 connector). Never call the OC200 by LAN IP. Never invent Omada endpoints, headers, cookies, or token formats.
- Never expose Paystack or Omada secrets. Do not log voucher codes, passwords, tokens, cookies, or session IDs.
- Financial amounts are integer kobo. Schema changes require Prisma migrations.
- Guest checkout must remain possible. Do not require registration to buy.
- After a phase, run `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, and `npm test`.
